@startuml
title Modified Local File Upload Flow
start

note right
  This path is reached after a tracked local file has been identified
  as modified. Under ~--local-first it may run before the general
  online reconciliation pass, but local-first does not authorise a
  blind overwrite of independently changed online content.
end note

:Resolve canonical or remote/shared target DriveItem identity;
:Fetch latest online metadata and eTag where possible;
:Read local file size and choose provisional upload method;

if (~--upload-only + ~--local-first or force_session_upload?) then (yes)
  :Force upload-session path;
endif

if (Current online metadata is available?) then (yes)
  :Evaluate current online state against\nlocal file and last applied DB baseline;
  note right
    CONFLICT-PROTECTION BOUNDARY

    The client checks current online state before local bytes are
    allowed to replace the online canonical file. The exact proof
    used to classify a genuine online change belongs to reconciliation
    policy, not to simple-versus-session upload transport.
  end note
  if (Online conflict requires preserving local version?) then (yes)
    :Create verified independent safeBackup copy;
    note right
      LOCAL DATA LOSS PREVENTION

      Preserve the local modification before conflict resolution.
      This prevents a genuine online change from causing the local
      user's different content to be silently discarded.
    end note
    if (Preservation succeeds?) then (yes)
      :Upload safeBackup as a new file;
      note right
        The preserved local version becomes an independent online file,
        while the original online canonical item is left untouched.
      end note
      if (~--upload-only?) then (yes)
        :Retain canonical local file;
        note right
          In upload-only operation the client does not download the
          conflicting online canonical version back over the local path.
        end note
      else (no)
        :Apply current online canonical file via\ntransactional download;
        note right
          In bidirectional operation the current online canonical can
          now be applied locally because the differing local version
          has been safely preserved first.
        end note
      endif
    else (no)
      :Preservation failed; keep original local data;
      note right
        Required preservation failed, so the original local file must
        not be used to overwrite the conflicting online canonical item.
      end note
    endif
    :Do not overwrite online canonical with original local file;
    stop
  endif
endif

if (Zero-byte or simple-upload-sized file?) then (yes)
  :simpleUploadReplace();
else (no)
  :Create resumable upload session using current eTag;
  :Upload file fragments / resume as required;
endif

:Return upload response to higher-level\npost-upload integrity / timestamp reconciliation;
stop
@enduml
